<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sa'ad ad-Din II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">executed c. 1410</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sa'ad ad-Din II was the last ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ifat-sultanate">Ifat Sultanate</a>, a Muslim state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walashma-dynasty">Walashma dynasty</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horn-of-africa">Horn of Africa</a>. He was captured and executed around 1410 during the campaigns of the Ethiopian Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dawit-i">Dawit I</a>, forcing his surviving family into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adal-sultanate">Adal Sultanate</a> profile notes that his sons returned to found the Adal Sultanate, and the region of Adal was later associated with his name.</p></div>
